<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ui version="4.0">
 <class>ThymioConfigForm</class>
 <widget class="QWidget" name="ThymioConfigForm">
  <property name="geometry">
   <rect><x>0</x><y>0</y><width>420</width><height>240</height></rect>
  </property>
  <layout class="QFormLayout" name="form_layout">
   <property name="leftMargin"><number>0</number></property>
   <property name="topMargin"><number>0</number></property>
   <property name="rightMargin"><number>0</number></property>
   <property name="bottomMargin"><number>0</number></property>
   <item row="0" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="id_label">
     <property name="text"><string>Thymio ID:</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="0" column="1">
    <widget class="QLineEdit" name="id_edit">
     <property name="whatsThis"><string>This robot's name in the app and in settings.yaml (e.g. thymio-1). Sessions and logs refer to it by this ID.</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="2" column="1">
    <widget class="QCheckBox" name="wireless_check">
     <property name="text"><string>Drive wheels wirelessly</string></property>
     <property name="whatsThis"><string>Drive the Thymio's wheels and top LED from the app, wirelessly. Choose the transport below. When off, the Thymio's air-chamber skins still work; only the wheels/LEDs stay idle.</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="3" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="via_label">
     <property name="text"><string>Wireless via:</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="3" column="1">
    <widget class="QComboBox" name="via_combo">
     <property name="whatsThis"><string>How the app reaches the Thymio's wheels:
- RF dongle - thymiodirect straight to the wireless dongle's serial port (no Thymio Suite needed; one dongle relays to several Thymios by node id).
- Gateway C6 - the gateway's own C6 drives the Thymios over 802.15.4, NO dongle: the C6 impersonates the dongle and holds the link itself. Up to 4 Thymios per C6, told apart by the address below.</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="4" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="node_id_label">
     <property name="text"><string>Wireless node id:</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="4" column="1">
    <widget class="QSpinBox" name="node_id_spin">
     <property name="minimum"><number>0</number></property>
     <property name="maximum"><number>65535</number></property>
     <property name="specialValueText"><string>auto (first)</string></property>
     <property name="whatsThis"><string>Which Thymio on the shared RF dongle this robot is (dongle transport only). One dongle relays to several Thymios at once, each with its own wireless node id - give each robot a distinct id (list them with `scripts/thymio_jog.py --list`). 0 = auto: bind to the first Thymio the dongle reports (fine when only one is paired).</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="5" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="channel_label">
     <property name="text"><string>Channel (C6):</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="5" column="1">
    <widget class="QSpinBox" name="channel_spin">
     <property name="minimum"><number>11</number></property>
     <property name="maximum"><number>26</number></property>
     <property name="value"><number>25</number></property>
     <property name="whatsThis"><string>802.15.4 channel the Thymio is on (Gateway C6 transport only). Find it with `scripts/thymio_sniff_capture.py --scan`; it was 25 in testing.</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="6" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="addr_label">
     <property name="text"><string>Address (C6):</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="6" column="1">
    <layout class="QHBoxLayout" name="addr_row">
     <item>
      <widget class="QLineEdit" name="addr_edit">
       <property name="placeholderText"><string>auto / e.g. 6a25</string></property>
       <property name="whatsThis"><string>This Thymio's 802.15.4 short address in hex (e.g. 6a25) - how the C6 tells the robots apart (Gateway C6 transport). Leave blank for the first robot (uses the C6's built-in default). Use Discover to read the addresses off the air.</string></property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QPushButton" name="discover_btn">
       <property name="text"><string>Discover...</string></property>
       <property name="whatsThis"><string>Find this robot's address over the air - no dongle. Opens a guided scan: the gateway asks the network who is there and every powered robot answers with its address; pick this robot's from the live list. Only finds robots already paired to this network. Needs the gateway connected.</string></property>
      </widget>
     </item>
     <item>
      <widget class="QPushButton" name="cable_btn">
       <property name="text"><string>From cable...</string></property>
       <property name="whatsThis"><string>Read this robot's address straight off its USB cable - no dongle, no network. Plug the Thymio into the PC with its micro-USB cable and press this: it reads the robot's id over USB and fills the address. Use it for a brand-new robot that isn't on this network yet (wireless Discover can't see those). Close Thymio Suite first so it doesn't hold the port.</string></property>
      </widget>
     </item>
    </layout>
   </item>
   <item row="7" column="0">
    <widget class="QLabel" name="impact_label">
     <property name="text"><string>Impact threshold (C6):</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item row="7" column="1">
    <widget class="QDoubleSpinBox" name="impact_spin">
     <property name="decimals"><number>0</number></property>
     <property name="minimum"><double>1.000000000000000</double></property>
     <property name="maximum"><double>500.000000000000000</double></property>
     <property name="singleStep"><double>5.000000000000000</double></property>
     <property name="value"><double>20.000000000000000</double></property>
     <property name="whatsThis"><string>How hard a knock counts as an "impact" for the on_impact behaviour block (Gateway C6 transport). It's the accelerometer's deviation from rest; lower = more sensitive. Calibrate it live in Test Thymio by knocking the robot and watching the impact bar.</string></property>
    </widget>
   </item>
  </layout>
 </widget>
 <resources/>
 <connections/>
</ui>
